WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:17.910 align:start position:0%
 
four  environmentally friendly lawn mowers at  work for the city of paris  the sheep keep the grass short on  undeveloped plots of land  without endangering the small animals  living there  the sheba currently grazing on a lot  near the city archives  the head of the archives herself and  animal lover brought them here  she hopes the sheik will prove to be  more than insect-friendly lawn groomers  people don't know us we're back from the  street and the way isn't well signposted  it was designed that way for security  reasons the sheep help us to show people  look here's some green space perfect for  a picnic  and if you're a little curious you can  take a peek in our conference room  naturally these aren't run-of-the-mill  domestic sheep  next to choice cows and pigs they're  bred here at this farm operated by the  city of paris  this breed of breton dwarf sheep was  once virtually extinct  these sheep stay small so you can forget  using them for meat  but they have other benefits they're  robust  and almost never get sick and they eat  everything imaginable  even plants with little protein  until now cars not animals had priority  in paris  even the banks of the river sen were  paved to facilitate the flow of traffic  pollution became so bad that parisians  decided to take action  many voted for the green party in the  last local elections  far more than usually do in france  the green city councillors declared war  on traffic and began cultivating green  spaces in the city  now they're basking in their success  the city has even become a place of  refuge for various animal species  the agricultural areas surrounding the  city are so contaminated with pesticides  that the animals prefer to come to paris  foxes in particular are often seen in  the city  and species like the soprano pipistrelle  a bat once rare in paris  find the french capital increasingly  attractive  even the timetable of construction work  has been altered on their account  at this construction site they work day  and night for months to be finished  before winter set in  now around 500 of the little bats can  hibernate here undisturbed by the  vibrations of construction equipment  few parisians ever come face to face  with a soprano pepestral  this one was nursed back to health by a  parisian student  after it broke its wing  but for animal rights activists the  city's animal protection initiatives  don't go far enough  they say some animals are getting a  rough deal  the city council doesn't like stray cats  a few years ago there were lots of  untagged cats in my district  but then the city sent out animal  catchers and from one day to the next  the cats were gone  except for mara here who i rescued when  there are too many of one kind of animal  people get frightened  especially people at city hall  at paris city hall staff say they've  done nothing wrong  it's part of the concept that the  numbers of any single species  shouldn't get out of hand that's why  peregrine falcons have been brought in  to drive out many of the thousands of  pigeons now living in paris  in june atop a smokestack at a paris  heating plant  a brood of peregrine chicks was born a  first for the city  if you told me a decade ago that there'd  be peregrines in paris  i'd never have believed it they're birds  that normally  only live in the wild  residents seem to appreciate the  initiative more animals in paris  albeit with certain reservations  the pigeons are a nuisance but they've  been largely exterminated in paris  so things are much better now as long as  they don't make a mess  other animals don't bother me  in parkland that's good then you don't  need to mow the grass  they're wild animals in the city like  squirrels  those kind of animals okay as long as  they don't hurt us  one of the world's oldest taxidermist  shops they say that animals are  currently fashionable in paris  interior decorators are clamoring for  prepared and stuffed animals  the britain dwarf sheep is still missing  from their extensive collection of  mounted animals  but then these woolly creatures are  still needed alive  elsewhere

